                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-dove"></i> Outdoor Mindfulness</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Built by the Cornell Lab of Ornithology, <a href="https://www.merlinbirds.org/download/" target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer">Merlin Bird ID</a> is a wonderful secret weapon for parents who want
                  technology to slow their children down. Using its live "Sound ID" feature requires standing completely
                  still and quiet outdoors for 30 to 60 seconds so the microphone can hear nearby birds singing in the
                  trees.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <strong>Why families love it:</strong> Watching the app identify a robin, wren, or warbler in real time
                  turns a backyard or park walk into a shared mindfulness exercise. It is 100% free, non-profit, and
                  reconnects children's senses with the real world.
                </p>
              </div>

