                  farmhouse, toddlers and preschoolers visit each lit room in the barn and tap the light switch to tuck
                  sleepy animals (a dog, pig, sheep, duck, cow, and little fish) into bed.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <strong>Why families love it:</strong> Accompanied by a gentle lullaby and a warm, unhurried
                  storyteller voice in multiple languages, each animal yawns, stretches, and curls up to sleep as the
                  lights go out. Because the story naturally ends when the entire farm is dark and fast asleep, it
                  creates the ultimate peaceful stopping point before bedtime.
                </p>
